# 08-SPD / page speed

**Goes here.** Performance. Field versus lab metrics, LCP, INP, CLS, app and plugin
script weight, image and font strategy, render blocking, how to measure, and what
each fix is worth.

## Not here

- Initial theme and app configuration -> 05-SET
- Whether a speed fix moved conversion -> 09-CRO
- Hosting security, WAF and bot traffic -> 23-SEC

## Header

```
---
url:                   # REQUIRED. Never blank.
rights: public_reference
why:
modules: [SPD]
platform: []           # [shopify] or [woocommerce] where the advice does not transfer
topics: []
tier: 1                # prefer web.dev and Chrome documentation
scope_hint: baseline
---
```

`platform` matters here more than almost anywhere else. Shopify is hosted, so the
levers are theme code and app scripts. WooCommerce is self-hosted, so hosting, caching
and plugin bloat are a whole extra surface. Keep 1 WooCommerce speed source, not more.

## Topics

field versus lab metrics, LCP, INP, CLS, app script weight, image and font strategy,
render blocking, measurement method.

## Look for

Field metrics versus lab metrics and when each applies. Thresholds. The order to fix
things in. What each fix typically buys. How to measure app or plugin script weight,
because that usually sits at the top of the ranked list once priced.

## Skip

**Lighthouse score chasing.** Anything treating the score as the goal rather than a
diagnostic. Gate every recommendation on field data at the 75th percentile.

**Tool tutorials** that walk the PageSpeed Insights interface. Keep only the parts
about reading field data.

**Statistics listicles** unless every statistic carries its sample and source. Most
"page speed statistics" pages recycle the same few figures without either.

**Generic speed guides.** Several near-identical ecommerce speed guides exist here.
Keep 2: the most operator-facing and the most specific.

## The unit that matters

Convert milliseconds into orders per month. Speed reports lose arguments because they
are written in milliseconds and read by people who think in orders. A source giving
conversion effect per millisecond by template is worth 10 that give a checklist.

## Scope mix

Nearly all baseline. Speed advice barely varies by brand, which makes this the
cheapest module to build well.

